  "query_preview": "(Saturday night through Wednesday)...\nChances for precipitation will increase from Saturday afternoon \ninto Saturday night with the most likely time for any heavier \nrainfall for late Saturday night into Sunday morning. The most \nlikely rainfall through 11 PM Saturday is around 0.10 inch. \n\nFor Saturday morning through Sunday night, from the coast to the\nmountains, the chance for 0.10 inch or more of rainfall ranges \nfrom 75 percent in eastern Los Angeles County to 85 percent for \nsouthern San Diego County. The chance for 1 inch or more of \nrainfall ranges from 35 to 40 percent for eastern Los Angeles \nCounty to 55 to 65 percent for southern San Diego County. \n\nCluster analysis shows ensemble members of the GFS are decidedly \ndrier than those of the ECMWF and Canadian models with little \noverlap with the ensemble members of those two other ensemble\nsystems. \n\nA warming trend is expected for Monday through Wednesday of next \nweek with high temperatures warming to around average on Tuesday.\nMonday and Tuesday are expected to be dry. There is around a 10 \nto 15 percent chance for light precipitation around next \nWednesday from a low pressure system moving into northern and \ncentral California.",
